# MedBook – Appointment Booking System

MedBook is a simple web-based doctor appointment booking system.  
The project demonstrates a full-stack architecture using **Node.js**, **Express**, **MongoDB Atlas**, and a small **frontend UI** built with HTML/CSS/JavaScript

Team
Aida Kentay – SE-2428
Tomiris Kassymova – SE-2428

##  Live Deployment (Production)
**URL:** https://medbook-mongo2.onrender.com

The application supports full CRUD functionality through the web interface — no Postman needed during defense.


## Project Features

✔ Full CRUD operations for appointments  
✔ REST API using Express  
✔ MongoDB as a database (Atlas in production)  
✔ Frontend UI using Fetch API  
✔ Deployed to production (Render)  
✔ Environment variables for secure configuration  
✔ Clean and simple user interface  

---

##  Data Model (MongoDB)

Each appointment contains:

```json
{
  "patientName": "Aida",
  "doctorName": "Dr. Brown",
  "date": "2026-02-01 10:00"
}
Documents are stored in the appointments collection.

API Endpoints (Backend)
Method	Endpoint	Description
GET	/api/appointments	Get all appointments
GET	/api/appointments/:id	Get appointment by id
POST	/api/appointments	Create an appointment
PUT	/api/appointments/:id	Update appointment
DELETE	/api/appointments/:id	Delete appointment

Frontend (Production UI)
The UI allows users to:

 View appointments in a table
 Create new appointments (form)
 Update existing appointments
 Delete appointments

All actions communicate with the backend using the Fetch API.

Environment Variables
Local .env example:
ini

PORT=3000
MONGO_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/medbook
JWT_SECRET=secret_value_here
Production (Render):
Configured in Render dashboard:

PORT

MONGO_URI

JWT_SECRET

.env is not pushed to GitHub for security reasons.

Technologies Used
